  "id": "Compound::DB00536 - Gene::3744",
  "verbalization": "Guanidine exhibits a strong binding interaction with multiple potassium channel subunits, specifically Kcnc3, Kcna7, and Kcnv2, all of which are involved in delayed rectifier potassium channel activity. This activity is ultimately linked to the participation of Kcna10, suggesting a potential mechanistic pathway where Guanidine modulates potassium channel function through binding and subsequent activation of delayed rectifier channels. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust and reliable relationship, with Guanidine acting as a modulator of Kcna10 through its interaction with these channels. The evidence supports a direct influence of Guanidine on Kcna10 via the delayed rectifier potassium channel pathway, highlighting a potential role in cellular electrophysiology. The mechanism is supported by the presence of a well-documented pathway involving Kcna10, and the binding of Guanidine to multiple related channels suggests a general effect on potassium channel function.",
